  m_text: "Headline: Crestwood Mansion\u2019s Dark Legacy: Three Families and Their Staff Found Dead in Chilling Circumstances\n\nDate: April 10, 1970\n\nArticle:\n\nThe recent murder of Jonathan Hayes, his family, and the mansion staff has rekindled interest in the sinister history of Crestwood Mansion, a place where tragedy seems to strike with disturbing regularity. The Hayes family is now the third to meet a gruesome end in the mansion's walls, but they are not alone in their fate. All three families, along with their household staff, were found dead under mysterious circumstances, leaving locals to wonder if something more sinister is at play.\n\nThe first tragedy occurred in 1935 when the mansion\u2019s original owners, the Whitfield family, were discovered dead in their bedrooms, alongside their staff. Investigators initially classified the deaths as a murder-suicide, but whispers of foul play and unexplained occurrences persisted long after the case was closed.\n\nSeventeen years later, in 1952, the Lennox family\u2014new owners of Crestwood\u2014were found dead, along with their butler and maids, in the mansion\u2019s grand dining hall. No signs of forced entry were ever found, and the case grew cold, fueling rumors of a curse tied to the estate."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 79af5aa2d9f81be4080184a80363fcfc, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6467807135178674435, guid: 79af5aa2d9f81be4080184a80363fcfc, type: 2}
